spans.s:
प्र-√ चक्ष् Ā. -चष्टे, to tell, relate, declare, MBh.; Ragh.;
to suppose, regard or consider as (acc.), Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to name, call, Mn.; BhP. :
Caus. -चक्षयति, to irradiate, illumine, RV.

प्र-√ चर् P. -चरति (ep. also Ā. ˚ते), to proceed towards, go or come to, arrive at (acc.), RV. &c. &c.;
to come forth, appear, MBh.; R. &c.;
to roam, wander, Prab.; BhP.;
to circulate, be or become current (as a story), R.; Var.;
to set about, perform, discharge (esp. sacred functions, with instr. of the object or of the means employed), AV.; Br.; KātyŚr.;
to be active or busy, be occupied or engaged in (loc.), MBh.; BhP.;
to proceed, behave, act in peculiar manner, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to come off, take place, BhP. :
Caus. -चारयति, to allow to roam, turn out to graze, Hariv.;
to make public, W.

प्र-√ चल् P. -चलति (rarely Ā. ˚ते), to be set in motion, tremble, quake, TBr.; MBh. &c.;
to stir, move on, advance, set out, depart, MBh.; BhP.; Pañcat.;
to start, spring up from (a seat), R.;
to swerve, deviate from (abl.), MBh.;
to become troubled or confused, be perplexed or bewildered or excited, ib.; BhP. :
Caus. -चलयति, to set in motion, move, jog, wag, Kāv.;
to remove from (abl.), Suśr.;
 -चालयति, to cause to shake or tremble, R.;
to stir up, stir round, Pañcat.

प्र-√ 1. चि P. Ā. -चिनोति, -चिनुते, to collect, gather, pluck, Gobh.; MBh. &c.;
to mow or cut down (enemies), MBh.;
to increase, augment, enhance, Var. :
Pass. -चीयते, to be gathered or collected, to grow, thrive, multiply, MBh.; Kāv.

प्र-√ चित् P. Ā. -चिकेत्ति, -चिकित्ते, to know or make known, RV.;
to become visible or manifest, appear, ib.; TS. :
Caus. -चेतयति, to make known, cause to appear, RV.;
 (Ā.) to appear, ib. :
Desid. -चिकित्सति, to show, point out, ib.

प्र-√ चुद् P. -चोदति, to set in motion, drive on, urge, impel, RV. :
Caus. -चोदयति id., RV. (Ā. to hasten, make haste, viii, 24, 13), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to excite, inspire, RV.;
to command, summon, request, demand, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to announce, make known, proclaim, Mn. iii, 228.

P. Ā. -च्छादयति, ˚ते to cover, envelop, wrap up (Ā. with instr. ‘to cover one's self with, put on’), ŚBr.; GṛŚrS.; MBh. &c.;
to be in the way, be an obstacle to (acc.), R.;
to hide, conceal, disguise, keep secret, Mn.; MBh. &c.

प्र-√ च्यु Ā. -च्यवते (ep. also P. ˚ति), to move, proceed, depart, TS.; AV.; ŚBr.;
to swerve or deviate from (abl.), MBh.;
to be deprived of, lose (abl.), ib.; Kāv.; Pañcat.;
to come or stream forth, ib.;
to fall down, drop, stumble, ŚBr.; MBh.; R.;
to fall (scil. from heaven i.e. be born again), HPariś. :
Caus. -च्यावयति, to move, shake, RV.;
to eject, remove or dispel or divert from (abl.), ib. &c. &c.;
to cause to fall (lit. and fig.), MBh.; Daś.; BhP.; Suśr.
